// Libre AI Biscuit authority block template v2.
// Extends v1 with the loop-security kernel K1 agent identity taxonomy
// (docs/specifications/LOOP-SECURITY-KERNEL.md, section K1, realized at the
// orchestrator lock). Values are issuer-side parameters. No PII or content is
// permitted.
//
// Human and browser-session tokens continue to use the v1 authority block.
// Agent-fleet tokens (the self-feeding loop, opened at the wave-3 lock) use this
// v2 block, which carries the three K1 identity facts.

user({user});
tenant({tenant});
role({user}, {role});

// K1 identity taxonomy — the three agent facts of LOOP-SECURITY-KERNEL.md K1.
// agent_fleet: every agent belongs to exactly one fleet (e.g. forge, product-ops).
// mission_agent: the mission the agent operates within (agent-side identity).
// capability_scope: the explicit permission vector (which tools, which write
// paths; CI and gates are never granted by default).
agent_fleet({agent}, {fleet});
mission_agent({agent}, {mission});
capability_scope({agent}, {capability});

// An agent token must carry its identity facts, or it holds no authority.
check if agent_fleet($agent, $fleet);
check if mission_agent($agent, $mission);

// Expiry (unchanged from v1).
check if time($time), $time < {expires_at};

// ── Enforcement status: what this template guarantees vs. what is deferred ──
//
// CONFIRMED by the socle today:
// - Per-agent_id revocation, fail-closed. This template carries no
//   token-supplied revocation identifier (the contract gate forbids one), so
//   revocation is keyed on agent_id: a revoked agent issues no new tokens and an
//   unavailable revocation store denies. Consistent with the G1 Biscuit doctrine.
//
// DEFERRED to the authorizer-wiring increment — NOT enforced by this template:
// - Cross-fleet and cross-mission isolation is NOT yet in force. The current
//   agent-runs authorizer (contracts/authz/agent-runs-v1.datalog) checks
//   token_mission / resource_mission and roles, but does NOT consume agent_fleet
//   or mission_agent. Until a successor authorizer (agent-runs v2) adds `check
//   if` clauses over agent_fleet and mission_agent, these facts are identity
//   metadata, not an enforced boundary. Tracked as a backlog precondition of
//   promotion to `locked` (docs/reviews/authority-v2/REVIEW-PACKAGE.md,
//   STATUS.md "Explicitly deferred").
// - capability_scope validation is a crate responsibility (checked at the
//   tool/write-path boundary). The block encodes the fact; it does not validate
//   the capability set, and never grants CI or gate write by default.
//
// AUTHORIZER COMPATIBILITY (issuance requirement, not part of K1 identity):
// - agent-runs-v1 additionally requires a token_mission fact at authorization
//   time. authz-biscuit injects it during issuance as the per-token operating
//   mission — distinct from the mission_agent identity fact above. The wiring
//   increment must bind the per-token operating mission to the agent's
//   mission_agent set (token operates only within a mission the agent belongs to).
